1
00:00:00,554 --> 00:00:02,472
It's you!

2
00:00:03,724 --> 00:00:06,309
-The devil!
-You're wrong!

3
00:00:06,393 --> 00:00:07,978
No devil. Riri.

4
00:00:08,061 --> 00:00:09,229
Hoshino.

5
00:00:10,897 --> 00:00:12,065
Huh…

6
00:00:16,153 --> 00:00:19,614
What are you two-- Why are you--
How long were you both there?

7
00:00:19,698 --> 00:00:22,200
I'm sorry, I wasn't trying to eavesdrop.

8
00:00:22,701 --> 00:00:24,619
-I fully was.
-Dude.

9
00:00:25,328 --> 00:00:27,914
I saw you following those two.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,754
I was just gonna step in
if it started to get bad.

11
00:00:33,837 --> 00:00:34,838
But, um, I…

12
00:00:35,589 --> 00:00:38,884
I never really found the right time to.

13
00:00:38,967 --> 00:00:42,387
You can tell me. I get it.
I'm so conscious about mine, too.

14
00:00:42,471 --> 00:00:44,890
But with yours, you worked magic,

15
00:00:44,973 --> 00:00:47,851
they look like a full C cup,
not like Anzu's at all.

16
00:00:48,435 --> 00:00:52,189
I'm so jealous of your push-up C cup.
C cup, C cup, C cup…

17
00:00:52,856 --> 00:00:54,357
C cup!

18
00:00:54,441 --> 00:00:56,318
Oh, my God!

19
00:00:56,985 --> 00:00:58,278
That's too high.

20
00:00:59,196 --> 00:01:00,655
Sorry about all that.

21
00:01:00,739 --> 00:01:03,867
Huh? Wait, what? Oh, it's not a big deal.

22
00:01:04,367 --> 00:01:05,202
And…

23
00:01:05,911 --> 00:01:06,828
Hm.

24
00:01:07,496 --> 00:01:09,414
Well, thank you again.

25
00:01:10,457 --> 00:01:13,877
Kazuki told me
he is not looking to date right now.

26
00:01:14,753 --> 00:01:17,881
Out of respect for my friend,
I can't help.

27
00:01:19,466 --> 00:01:20,383
Huh?

28
00:01:23,804 --> 00:01:24,971
What do you mean?

29
00:01:25,514 --> 00:01:29,434
All that C cup talk
completely distracted you.

30
00:01:30,018 --> 00:01:33,438
Anzu, is… is this girl here
a friend from your class?

31
00:01:33,522 --> 00:01:35,565
It's nice to meet you!

32
00:01:35,649 --> 00:01:38,735
I am Riri Fushigi, Anzu's cousin.

33
00:01:39,736 --> 00:01:41,655
-Cousin?
-That's right.

34
00:01:41,738 --> 00:01:45,283
Oh, Anzu told me so much
about both of you guys.

35
00:01:45,367 --> 00:01:47,119
You are her temp roomie, Kazuki.

36
00:01:47,202 --> 00:01:49,955
And you're her old friend, Junta.
Is that right?

37
00:01:50,622 --> 00:01:53,125
Now, let's all head home together.

38
00:01:53,208 --> 00:01:54,126
Huh?

39
00:01:54,209 --> 00:01:56,461
Talk about fate,
us all meeting like this.

40
00:01:56,545 --> 00:01:59,047
Hey, the four of us
should totally have a dinner party.

41
00:01:59,131 --> 00:02:00,841
At Anzu's place, of course.

42
00:02:00,924 --> 00:02:02,592
She's not gonna stop.

43
00:02:02,676 --> 00:02:05,262
You don't have to work tonight, right?

44
00:02:05,345 --> 00:02:06,513
Uh, yeah.

45
00:02:07,013 --> 00:02:09,641
And, Junta, you don't have
baseball practice, right?

46
00:02:09,724 --> 00:02:10,725
Right.

47
00:02:10,809 --> 00:02:12,811
Then let's hurry home!

48
00:02:14,146 --> 00:02:15,981
Come on, I'm starving.

49
00:02:16,064 --> 00:02:16,982
Huh, huh…

50
00:02:17,065 --> 00:02:19,442
-Hooray! Let's go!
-Hey! Wait!

51
00:02:19,526 --> 00:02:20,819
BULLDOZING HER WAY THROUGH

52
00:02:20,902 --> 00:02:23,905
Your magic's been
a whole lot of trouble,

53
00:02:23,989 --> 00:02:26,283
but you're way
more trouble to me in flesh and blood.

54
00:04:00,252 --> 00:04:03,255
That's right.
In order to save Junta,

55
00:04:03,338 --> 00:04:05,340
who's unfortunately in love with me,

56
00:04:05,924 --> 00:04:07,425
just because of that devil,

57
00:04:07,509 --> 00:04:11,930
and for my own sake as well,
I've gotta crush those feels!

58
00:04:12,013 --> 00:04:14,516
So let's tuck in that shirt.

59
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:17,519
No, not today!

60
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:23,441
Riri! When did you…

61
00:04:24,025 --> 00:04:26,444
I'm so happy!

62
00:04:26,528 --> 00:04:29,948
You called me by my real name
for the very first time.

63
00:04:30,031 --> 00:04:32,117
I don't care about all that.

64
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:35,328
When did you decide to take human shape?

65
00:04:35,412 --> 00:04:38,456
What happened to
your way less cute body, huh?

66
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:40,500
-I'm here for support.
-Huh?

67
00:04:41,084 --> 00:04:45,255
Anzu, you're destroying
your chance of getting close to Junta,

68
00:04:45,338 --> 00:04:48,508
your second personally selected
hot potential boyfriend.

69
00:04:48,591 --> 00:04:53,471
That's why I thought I would step it up
and help you in person!

70
00:04:54,055 --> 00:04:55,473
And with my support,

71
00:04:55,557 --> 00:04:58,977
your two-hottie dinner party
will be super successful.

72
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:02,314
So now, go change into
a cuter, more girly outfit!

73
00:05:02,397 --> 00:05:04,858
And don't part your hair like that.

74
00:05:04,941 --> 00:05:07,694
Shut up! I look just fine like this!

75
00:05:07,777 --> 00:05:11,156
No way. You look lame like that.
They'll be totally turned off.

76
00:05:14,242 --> 00:05:17,120
Let's try a little harder! Huh?

77
00:05:17,203 --> 00:05:19,622
It's fine if they are turned off.

78
00:05:30,258 --> 00:05:31,092
Open.

79
00:05:32,886 --> 00:05:34,220
Ow!

80
00:05:34,888 --> 00:05:36,973
Hm…

81
00:05:37,057 --> 00:05:37,891
Huh?

82
00:05:40,894 --> 00:05:43,897
Our roles
have been reversed once again.

83
00:05:48,485 --> 00:05:49,694
Sorry.

84
00:05:52,947 --> 00:05:56,618
I feel like weird stuff happens
when I'm with you.

85
00:05:56,701 --> 00:05:57,702
Sorry.

86
00:06:03,291 --> 00:06:06,586
You jerk!
That was all part of your scheme.

87
00:06:09,172 --> 00:06:10,507
Thanks for the invite.

88
00:06:11,007 --> 00:06:13,218
Here, my mom made karaage.

89
00:06:13,301 --> 00:06:15,553
Wow, thank you!

90
00:06:16,304 --> 00:06:19,516
-Karaage! Karaage! Karaage!
-Is that curry?

91
00:06:19,599 --> 00:06:21,101
-Karaage!
-Smells good!

92
00:06:21,184 --> 00:06:24,687
Yep! Kazuki is making it right now.

93
00:06:26,147 --> 00:06:28,149
Let's eat!

94
00:06:34,781 --> 00:06:37,283
So good!

95
00:06:37,367 --> 00:06:38,368
What's in it?

96
00:06:38,868 --> 00:06:40,787
I added asparagus juice.

97
00:06:40,870 --> 00:06:42,789
Mm… amazing!

98
00:06:42,872 --> 00:06:45,375
I think it's even better
than my mom's curry.

99
00:06:45,458 --> 00:06:47,585
Hey, Junta, isn't it tasty?

100
00:06:47,669 --> 00:06:48,503
Yeah.

101
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:55,718
He's good-looking,
he's smart, and he's a great cook.

102
00:06:55,802 --> 00:06:57,929
I'm totally losing to him.

103
00:06:59,139 --> 00:07:02,809
Junta seems to be unaware
of his own awesome qualities.

104
00:07:07,647 --> 00:07:08,731
More, please.

105
00:07:08,815 --> 00:07:09,941
Really?

106
00:07:10,024 --> 00:07:11,151
Sure. Go on and get some.

107
00:07:11,234 --> 00:07:12,569
How much can I take?

108
00:07:12,652 --> 00:07:14,779
Help yourself. I made plenty for us.

109
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:18,700
Oh, you did, huh?
Then, I might have seconds too.

110
00:07:18,783 --> 00:07:20,577
-Aren't you on a diet?
-Huh?

111
00:07:21,327 --> 00:07:24,998
Huh? Anzu, you're on a diet? But why?

112
00:07:26,416 --> 00:07:31,045
Well, I… I am… just chocolate.
I'm trying to cut back on it a bit.

113
00:07:31,129 --> 00:07:33,631
Your favorite video games,
chocolate, your cat.

114
00:07:33,715 --> 00:07:37,510
Your three greatest desires
have all been confiscated by yours truly.

115
00:07:37,594 --> 00:07:39,804
But it's so yummy. Mm.

116
00:07:39,888 --> 00:07:41,514
I know you confiscated it.

117
00:07:41,598 --> 00:07:45,101
You would even eat tons of chocolate
when you had cavities and it made you cry.

118
00:07:45,602 --> 00:07:47,437
Did that even really happen?

119
00:07:48,646 --> 00:07:50,565
I'm going for seconds. Yah.

120
00:07:50,648 --> 00:07:51,691
Go for it.

121
00:07:52,567 --> 00:07:57,697
Kazuki, you're really helping Anzu out
by cooking and being so responsible.

122
00:07:58,698 --> 00:08:02,202
Why don't you have him
stay for longer than a month?

123
00:08:02,285 --> 00:08:03,119
What?

124
00:08:03,203 --> 00:08:07,081
It's stressful and dangerous
for a girl to have to live all by herself.

125
00:08:08,208 --> 00:08:10,710
Riri, what are you saying?

126
00:08:10,793 --> 00:08:13,838
That would be a pain
in the butt for Kazuki.

127
00:08:13,922 --> 00:08:15,423
Why would it be?

128
00:08:15,507 --> 00:08:19,135
It would be easier on him,
financially too.

129
00:08:22,847 --> 00:08:24,807
Shut up, you…

130
00:08:27,602 --> 00:08:29,812
No, that would be
way too much to ask of her.

131
00:08:32,982 --> 00:08:36,110
I'm so glad
that Kazuki's got common sense.

132
00:08:36,611 --> 00:08:38,696
It serves you right,

133
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:40,240
you stupid, idiot devil.

134
00:08:40,323 --> 00:08:43,826
I'm sure you're worried
about Anzu too, right Junta?

135
00:08:43,910 --> 00:08:45,745
I know. There's another empty room.

136
00:08:45,828 --> 00:08:47,539
Why don't you live with her too?

137
00:08:47,622 --> 00:08:48,540
Huh?

138
00:08:48,623 --> 00:08:52,544
Someone shut her up!
It's about to be a total chaos over here!

139
00:08:53,253 --> 00:08:56,548
I think I'm in the mood
for some ice cream now.

140
00:08:56,631 --> 00:08:58,132
-What? That's random!
-Hey!

141
00:08:58,216 --> 00:09:01,511
Rock-paper-scissors,
and the two losers go get it.

142
00:09:01,594 --> 00:09:03,846
I'm sorry, what is that now? Hm?

143
00:09:05,348 --> 00:09:06,849
Hey, wait, that wand…

144
00:09:09,102 --> 00:09:10,895
That's how she casts her magic.

145
00:09:13,314 --> 00:09:14,774
-Riri!
-Uh-huh?

146
00:09:17,819 --> 00:09:20,113
There's a fly.

147
00:09:20,196 --> 00:09:22,907
Never mind. It was just some gunk.

148
00:09:22,991 --> 00:09:25,952
Oh, Anzu, you're such a meanie sometimes.

149
00:09:30,039 --> 00:09:32,458
Anzu, my-- my wand…

150
00:09:32,542 --> 00:09:36,129
You can't use your magic
without this wand, can you?

151
00:09:36,212 --> 00:09:38,756
I'm sure your intention
was to manipulate the game

152
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:43,636
so that I would end up hanging out alone
with either Kazuki or Junta.

153
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:47,515
But I won't let you.
You pushed your luck too far!

154
00:09:48,099 --> 00:09:50,643
Anyway, shouldn't the one
who's in the mood

155
00:09:50,727 --> 00:09:53,521
for ice cream be the one to go get it?

156
00:09:53,605 --> 00:09:55,898
That way, you can pick the ones you want.

157
00:09:55,982 --> 00:10:01,154
Oh, fine, I'll go with you
since you want it that bad!

158
00:10:01,738 --> 00:10:03,656
All right, let's go.

159
00:10:07,327 --> 00:10:10,538
Anzu, will you please
give me back my wand?

160
00:10:10,622 --> 00:10:12,332
There's no way, Riri!

161
00:10:12,415 --> 00:10:14,626
I think I'll put it
in my blender and puree it.

162
00:10:14,709 --> 00:10:16,127
No. Please, don't.

163
00:10:16,210 --> 00:10:19,255
If you want it back,
you'll have to get down on your knees

164
00:10:19,339 --> 00:10:22,759
and beg for it.
Then go right back to your planet.

165
00:10:22,842 --> 00:10:24,385
Uh…

166
00:10:24,469 --> 00:10:26,763
You really are an Anti-Heroine.

167
00:10:27,805 --> 00:10:29,015
Uh, it's fine.

168
00:10:29,098 --> 00:10:31,684
I can just reorder it
and have it delivered.

169
00:10:32,602 --> 00:10:35,813
Now, I've caught you off guard!

170
00:10:38,691 --> 00:10:39,525
Huh!

171
00:10:51,621 --> 00:10:52,789
Oh, man.

172
00:10:53,373 --> 00:10:55,875
If the wand gets contaminated,

173
00:10:55,958 --> 00:10:59,045
I can't use it again
until it gets purified.

174
00:11:00,129 --> 00:11:03,049
Oh, really? Well, that's disappointing.

175
00:11:10,139 --> 00:11:12,934
By the way,
you have nothing to worry about.

176
00:11:13,476 --> 00:11:15,019
Huh, what do you mean?

177
00:11:15,687 --> 00:11:19,357
You might have heard this from Hoshino,
but I'm not interested in dating.

178
00:11:20,358 --> 00:11:24,278
You must be worried that some strange guy
is staying with the girl you like.

179
00:11:24,362 --> 00:11:25,738
Huh?

180
00:11:27,323 --> 00:11:28,157
I got it.

181
00:11:28,241 --> 00:11:30,118
Why would you say
something like that?

182
00:11:30,868 --> 00:11:32,245
The girl I like…

183
00:11:32,995 --> 00:11:34,372
Well, it's true, right?

184
00:11:35,873 --> 00:11:38,835
No way! Is it really that obvious?

185
00:11:38,918 --> 00:11:41,379
And wait, does Anzu know about it too?

186
00:11:41,462 --> 00:11:44,298
I don't think so. She's kind of oblivious.

187
00:11:45,591 --> 00:11:49,053
That's why there's no way
I'd fall for her, so don't worry.

188
00:11:49,679 --> 00:11:52,098
You think Anzu has nothing to offer?

189
00:11:52,181 --> 00:11:53,641
No, that wasn't my point.

190
00:11:54,517 --> 00:11:55,601
Listen…

191
00:11:56,102 --> 00:11:59,355
You don't have to worry about it.
Hoshino only likes me as a friend too.

192
00:12:00,022 --> 00:12:03,359
Kazuki, you don't need
to worry about my feelings.

193
00:12:04,694 --> 00:12:06,612
It's not like I even really have a say.

194
00:12:07,363 --> 00:12:09,157
As long as Anzu's happy,

195
00:12:11,492 --> 00:12:12,535
then so am I.

196
00:12:13,244 --> 00:12:16,122
I just have to try to keep up with her.

197
00:12:16,789 --> 00:12:20,710
Jeez, why the heck
am I telling you all of this stuff?

198
00:12:20,793 --> 00:12:21,794
Seriously.

199
00:12:22,754 --> 00:12:23,921
We're back.

200
00:12:24,505 --> 00:12:26,174
We got all sorts of ice cream…

201
00:12:26,257 --> 00:12:27,800
…so let's dig in.

202
00:12:28,384 --> 00:12:30,678
Sorry, Anzu, I broke a plate.

203
00:12:30,762 --> 00:12:32,764
What? Are you okay?

204
00:12:32,847 --> 00:12:33,765
Yeah.

205
00:12:33,848 --> 00:12:36,768
Boo-hoo-hoo. My poor wand.

206
00:12:44,025 --> 00:12:45,276
Dinner was great, thanks.

207
00:12:45,359 --> 00:12:46,360
Mm-hm.

208
00:12:46,444 --> 00:12:49,155
Well, Kazuki's the one
who made most of the food.

209
00:12:49,238 --> 00:12:50,948
The ice cream was good too.

210
00:12:51,032 --> 00:12:53,534
Thank you,
but I just bought them at the store.

211
00:12:56,037 --> 00:12:58,080
Can I come for dinner again?

212
00:12:58,164 --> 00:12:59,874
Huh? Of course.

213
00:13:00,875 --> 00:13:03,669
Okay, I think I'm actually gonna run home.

214
00:13:03,753 --> 00:13:05,922
Amazing. Be safe.

215
00:13:06,005 --> 00:13:07,298
I will. See ya.

216
00:13:08,841 --> 00:13:12,261
I'm so exhausted.

217
00:13:13,262 --> 00:13:15,181
But it looks like I survived another day.

218
00:13:17,517 --> 00:13:21,187
Hey, Kazuki. Thanks for doing
all that at the last minute.

219
00:13:21,270 --> 00:13:22,647
Huh? Uh, sure.

220
00:13:24,941 --> 00:13:28,653
It's been a while
since I've had such a lively dinner.

221
00:13:30,196 --> 00:13:32,824
That's right. You live alone, don't you?

222
00:13:34,909 --> 00:13:35,743
Yeah.

223
00:13:38,579 --> 00:13:42,375
Now that I think about it,
maybe there's a good reason that

224
00:13:43,042 --> 00:13:44,877
he lives all by himself.

225
00:13:46,128 --> 00:13:49,632
There are tons of complicated
family situations out there.

226
00:13:49,715 --> 00:13:52,093
It's probably not polite
for me to ask him.

227
00:13:55,179 --> 00:13:57,849
I'm sure he's going
to tell me about it someday.

228
00:14:07,483 --> 00:14:08,401
What's that?

229
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:13,948
Hm?

230
00:14:16,784 --> 00:14:17,660
Uh-oh.

231
00:14:18,995 --> 00:14:21,163
What the heck are you doing?

232
00:14:21,247 --> 00:14:24,125
What were you gonna do
with my beloved treasures?

233
00:14:24,208 --> 00:14:27,086
Huh? What is this? Revenge from yesterday?

234
00:14:33,551 --> 00:14:35,094
-Bye!
-Hey!

235
00:14:35,177 --> 00:14:36,762
Wait… Ugh…

236
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:39,307
Oh, I, um…

237
00:14:39,974 --> 00:14:42,310
There was a bug. Morning.

238
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:47,523
Nice hair.

239
00:14:54,238 --> 00:14:56,032
Where's your old friend today?

240
00:14:56,115 --> 00:14:57,658
He's got morning practice.

241
00:14:57,742 --> 00:14:58,743
Gotcha.

242
00:15:02,538 --> 00:15:06,208
Oh, hey, you think it's cool
to walk to school together?

243
00:15:06,292 --> 00:15:09,420
No one else from school lives
around here. It should be fine.

244
00:15:09,503 --> 00:15:10,338
All right.

245
00:15:15,927 --> 00:15:17,762
I'm starving.

246
00:15:17,845 --> 00:15:19,680
I can't wait for lunch.

247
00:15:20,264 --> 00:15:21,933
Don't get caught eating early again.

248
00:15:22,516 --> 00:15:24,268
-Where's Makoto today?
-Hm?

249
00:15:24,352 --> 00:15:26,020
He slept in.

250
00:15:27,021 --> 00:15:28,064
Is he gonna make it?

251
00:15:28,147 --> 00:15:29,523
-I'm sure he will.
-Oh, hey!

252
00:15:29,607 --> 00:15:31,651
Isn't that your old friend, Junta?

253
00:15:32,818 --> 00:15:34,987
Hm? She's with Kazuki, dude.

254
00:15:35,571 --> 00:15:38,991
-This is bad, man. The girls love him.
-Yeah? Hey! What?

255
00:15:39,575 --> 00:15:41,077
Junta, what's up?

256
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:42,078
Good morning.

257
00:15:42,578 --> 00:15:44,330
You're working hard, huh?

258
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:48,584
Yep.

259
00:15:49,585 --> 00:15:51,504
Are those two together, then?

260
00:15:51,587 --> 00:15:54,173
No, they just live
in the same neighborhood.

261
00:15:54,256 --> 00:15:57,009
So, that's why you were
asking about him yesterday.

262
00:15:57,093 --> 00:15:58,761
No, it's not like that.

263
00:16:01,305 --> 00:16:04,266
Hey, Anzu, when did you
and Kazuki become friends?

264
00:16:05,184 --> 00:16:06,727
Oh, I, uh…

265
00:16:07,311 --> 00:16:08,896
You walked to school with him.

266
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:10,564
I'm dying to know,

267
00:16:10,648 --> 00:16:13,484
because he seems like
the type who's not into girls.

268
00:16:13,567 --> 00:16:17,571
Oh, no, uh, we just live
really close to each other. That's all.

269
00:16:17,655 --> 00:16:19,573
Sorry, I can't tell you anything.

270
00:16:19,657 --> 00:16:22,201
-Oh, my gosh, that is, like, so unfair!
-Oh, my gosh, that is, like, so unfair!

271
00:16:22,785 --> 00:16:25,037
Yeah, Kazuki and I
are really just friends.

272
00:16:25,121 --> 00:16:26,580
-Really?
-That's it?

273
00:16:27,790 --> 00:16:28,666
Y-- Yeah…

274
00:16:31,293 --> 00:16:32,586
Okey dokey.

275
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:35,840
Well, I have to say
this is very exciting for me.

276
00:16:35,923 --> 00:16:38,676
You're finally
in a romantic comedy situation

277
00:16:38,759 --> 00:16:40,344
for the first time ever.

278
00:16:40,428 --> 00:16:42,430
Saki, you are correct.

279
00:16:42,513 --> 00:16:44,932
No. I'm so jealous.

280
00:16:45,016 --> 00:16:47,059
You can't hog them all, okay?

281
00:16:49,145 --> 00:16:50,938
Oh, yeah, how's living alone?

282
00:16:51,689 --> 00:16:53,649
We should have a sleepover soon.

283
00:16:53,733 --> 00:16:54,984
I'm so in!

284
00:16:55,067 --> 00:16:57,445
Yeah, let's do it.

285
00:17:12,418 --> 00:17:13,627
I'm so sleepy.

286
00:17:15,129 --> 00:17:17,506
Since Kazuki has work tonight,

287
00:17:17,590 --> 00:17:20,259
I'm alone as long as Riri doesn't show up.

288
00:17:27,558 --> 00:17:29,435
Damn it! I'm sleepy but I want a game!

289
00:17:29,518 --> 00:17:31,103
I want chocolate!

290
00:17:31,187 --> 00:17:33,147
And Momohiki!

291
00:17:33,230 --> 00:17:35,149
I'll distract myself with a nap.

292
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:38,152
Momohiki…

293
00:17:38,235 --> 00:17:40,071
I'm home.

294
00:17:41,447 --> 00:17:43,908
You're back, Junta!

295
00:17:45,367 --> 00:17:46,702
You're sweaty!

296
00:17:46,786 --> 00:17:48,871
What did you say? Ah, take this!

297
00:17:48,954 --> 00:17:51,499
Junta, hon, could you drop this off
at Anzu's house

298
00:17:51,582 --> 00:17:54,210
right after you take your bath?
It's nikujaga.

299
00:17:55,044 --> 00:17:58,089
What? Again? Isn't it late?

300
00:17:58,172 --> 00:18:00,966
It's all right.
She can eat it tomorrow.

301
00:18:01,675 --> 00:18:04,678
But, Mom, he's just got back!

302
00:18:14,980 --> 00:18:17,566
It's dark. Guess I must have overslept.

303
00:18:17,650 --> 00:18:20,027
Hm? Huh?

304
00:18:20,111 --> 00:18:22,029
Is Kazuki back from work already?

305
00:18:24,865 --> 00:18:27,493
Hm, it's too soon for him to be back.

306
00:18:27,993 --> 00:18:31,455
So that means that thing is here again.

307
00:18:36,836 --> 00:18:40,631
Hey, you! I'll smash your head in,
you bastard!

308
00:18:44,218 --> 00:18:46,846
An underwear thief?

309
00:18:46,929 --> 00:18:49,557
What? You ignore the teen girl's room

310
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:52,184
and steal the mom underwear!

311
00:18:52,726 --> 00:18:55,104
Okay now, why did I say that?

312
00:18:55,604 --> 00:18:57,648
Huh? He's running!

313
00:19:01,152 --> 00:19:02,820
I wonder if she's home.

314
00:19:13,747 --> 00:19:16,125
Stop!

315
00:19:16,208 --> 00:19:17,251
Hey Junta!

316
00:19:17,334 --> 00:19:18,335
Who was that guy?

317
00:19:18,419 --> 00:19:20,129
-An underwear thief!
-What?

318
00:19:20,212 --> 00:19:22,715
Ugh, he's escaping! I need a cop.

319
00:19:26,218 --> 00:19:27,720
What? Junta?

320
00:19:29,263 --> 00:19:30,431
Is he gonna be okay?

321
00:19:37,354 --> 00:19:38,272
Don't move!

322
00:19:42,735 --> 00:19:45,779
Hey, there they are! Officer, right there!

323
00:19:53,370 --> 00:19:54,246
Huh?

324
00:19:55,998 --> 00:19:57,875
So, after all of that…

325
00:19:57,958 --> 00:20:00,127
Jeez. It's already so late.

326
00:20:00,211 --> 00:20:03,589
I'm sorry you came to bring me food
and got wrapped up in that whole mess.

327
00:20:03,672 --> 00:20:04,590
It's all good.

328
00:20:05,090 --> 00:20:08,093
But you, you really saved me, Junta.

329
00:20:08,177 --> 00:20:09,803
You're faster than lightning.

330
00:20:09,887 --> 00:20:11,555
That thief had terrible luck.

331
00:20:12,139 --> 00:20:14,642
I'm glad the police was able
to get here right away, too.

332
00:20:14,725 --> 00:20:15,559
Mm-hm.

333
00:20:16,268 --> 00:20:19,980
Ah, I forgot I just woke up
from a nap. Is my hair a disaster?

334
00:20:20,064 --> 00:20:21,857
What? No, not at all.

335
00:20:22,524 --> 00:20:23,567
It's really cu--

336
00:20:24,068 --> 00:20:25,527
Uh, it's really?

337
00:20:27,029 --> 00:20:28,822
Normal! It's totally normal!

338
00:20:28,906 --> 00:20:30,574
That's good.

339
00:20:30,658 --> 00:20:32,701
My hair kind of explodes when I sleep.

340
00:20:34,411 --> 00:20:37,748
I'm jealous of Saki's hair.
I wish I had hair like hers.

341
00:20:38,332 --> 00:20:40,751
Hey, listen.
I'm really glad nothing happened.

342
00:20:41,710 --> 00:20:44,338
If anything happened to you, I…

343
00:20:49,843 --> 00:20:50,719
Hm?

344
00:20:51,637 --> 00:20:53,222
I'll just run to the store.

345
00:20:53,305 --> 00:20:55,933
-You don't have to!
-You've got it all wrong.

346
00:20:56,558 --> 00:20:57,935
An underwear thief?

347
00:20:58,018 --> 00:20:58,852
Yeah.

348
00:20:59,395 --> 00:21:01,897
Well, it's a good thing
the guy didn't try to attack you.

349
00:21:02,398 --> 00:21:04,525
There are plenty of nut cases out there.

350
00:21:04,608 --> 00:21:06,485
Well, apparently.

351
00:21:07,569 --> 00:21:11,448
But I think the thief was probably
more scared of me then I was of him.

352
00:21:12,574 --> 00:21:15,661
Does that mean you said
something to threaten him, then?

353
00:21:18,706 --> 00:21:21,000
My bad, I know it's messed up.

354
00:21:21,083 --> 00:21:22,543
You think this is funny?

355
00:21:26,422 --> 00:21:28,007
Oh, my mom.

356
00:21:28,090 --> 00:21:29,842
-I got to take this.
-Of course.

357
00:21:30,801 --> 00:21:32,011
-Mom…
-Oh, hey,

358
00:21:32,094 --> 00:21:34,596
did you finish work
early today or something?

359
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,557
It was slow so they sent me home.

360
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:37,474
Oh, gotcha.

361
00:21:37,975 --> 00:21:41,270
By the way,
since the bedroom window's broken,

362
00:21:41,353 --> 00:21:43,439
could you sleep on the couch tonight?

363
00:21:44,148 --> 00:21:48,068
Well, as long as someone doesn't
fall asleep holding me down,

364
00:21:48,152 --> 00:21:49,361
we're cool.

365
00:21:49,945 --> 00:21:50,988
Huh?

366
00:21:52,448 --> 00:21:53,657
Hm…

367
00:21:55,909 --> 00:21:59,830
Well, I am actually very sorry I did that.

368
00:21:59,913 --> 00:22:02,166
What? Well, wait a minute!

369
00:22:02,249 --> 00:22:04,209
-I mean that's a little…
-Huh?

370
00:22:04,293 --> 00:22:06,211
Oh, okay, fine.
I'll give her the phone.

371
00:22:07,212 --> 00:22:10,132
Sorry about this, my mom wants to talk.

372
00:22:11,133 --> 00:22:12,801
Huh? Sure.

373
00:22:14,303 --> 00:22:17,473
-Hello?
-Anzu, it's been a while.

374
00:22:17,556 --> 00:22:19,641
I heard about what happened.

375
00:22:19,725 --> 00:22:20,934
Oh, it's fine.

376
00:22:21,018 --> 00:22:22,936
That must have been so scary.

377
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:24,646
Oh, well, yeah.

378
00:22:24,730 --> 00:22:26,565
I'm so worried about you, sweetie.

379
00:22:26,648 --> 00:22:28,108
You must be scared all by yourself.

380
00:22:28,192 --> 00:22:30,402
You should have
a bodyguard, don't you think?

381
00:22:31,695 --> 00:22:32,571
What now?

382
00:22:32,654 --> 00:22:35,115
It's too dangerous
for a girl to live alone.

383
00:22:35,199 --> 00:22:38,077
I'll lend you Junta for a while.

384
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:41,538
Look, our place is beyond cramped
with all my boys,

385
00:22:41,622 --> 00:22:43,499
and it's just a total mess.

386
00:22:43,582 --> 00:22:45,626
Use him all you want. I'll let Miyo know.

387
00:22:45,709 --> 00:22:46,710
My mom?

388
00:22:46,794 --> 00:22:49,171
Oh, I'm sorry. The baby is crying.

389
00:22:49,254 --> 00:22:50,923
I'll talk to you later, okay?

390
00:22:51,715 --> 00:22:55,344
Hm, this forced scenario…

391
00:22:55,427 --> 00:22:57,721
I'm having mad deja vu right now?

392
00:22:57,805 --> 00:23:00,641
Ding, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding.

393
00:23:00,724 --> 00:23:02,142
I knew it!

394
00:23:02,226 --> 00:23:05,604
So that means… Uh, no, no way!

395
00:23:05,687 --> 00:23:08,649
All three of us will be living together?

396
00:23:08,732 --> 00:23:11,151
-Please, be delicious.
-All right, this one's next.

397
00:23:11,235 --> 00:23:12,736
-Listen to this.
-Oh, what happened?

398
00:23:13,737 --> 00:23:16,657
-Why!
-Yes!

399
00:23:17,658 --> 00:23:19,326
A fanfare, please!

400
00:23:19,410 --> 00:23:21,412
And a big congratulations!

401
00:23:21,495 --> 00:23:23,789
Did you fall for my little trick?

402
00:23:23,872 --> 00:23:26,834
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

403
00:23:26,917 --> 00:23:30,587
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

404
00:23:30,671 --> 00:23:33,340
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

405
00:23:33,424 --> 00:23:35,717
Don't just let things be! Come on!

406
00:23:35,801 --> 00:23:38,387
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

407
00:23:38,470 --> 00:23:40,389
So I can make sure I get paid.

